        "title": "Flow Batteries: Architecture, Vanadium Redox, and Iron-Air",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "KEY ADVANTAGE -- SAME ELEMENT IN BOTH TANKS:\n  Cross-contamination does NOT permanently degrade electrolyte\n  If V2+ crosses membrane to VO2+ tank: both become a mix of V(II) and V(V)\n  -> Re-charge restores separation\n  Vs. other flow chemistries (Fe/Cr, Zn/Br): cross-contamination = irreversible contamination"
    },
